Codex turn reply reads (#8053)\n- Measure fragmented NDJSON incrementally (#8277)\n\n## Bug Fixes\n\n- Ship per-model effort ladders and fold native Chat ultra (#8259)\n- Bound Windows overflow slices and preserve child cleanup (#8229)\n- Hedge leftover-pin refusal and count in-flight readiness reads (#8261)\n- Bound tool-call validation and document request limits (#8147)\n- Preserve mandatory tool choices through routing and recovery (#8146)\n- Preserve late Devin signatures for DSH clients (#8230)\n- Batch affinity writes and confirm operator resets (#8020)\n- Enforce root send ceilings at physical admission (#8149)\n- Fix dashboard switch and combo layout regressions (#8269)\n- Fix clipped Models rows and dashboard control layout (#8272)\n- Accept unambiguous selected tool aliases (#8235)\n- Sanitize Chat fields and normalize native thinking content (#8278)\n- Fix omitted effort on dual-control Chat wires (#8279)\n- Honor max omission before native ultra clamping (#8284)\n- Align macOS traffic lights on Sequoia and keep chips rounded in WKWebView (#8285)\n- Fix launcher signal race and chat-completions network flake (#8289)\n- Keep masked account label validation linear (#8316)\n\n## Chores\n\n- Stabilize Windows fixture setup and source checks (#8176)\n- Isolate Codex CLI update fixture process scans (#8283)\n- Include uninstall refusal reason in regression output (#8242)\n\n## Other Changes\n\n- Open dev at 2.99.0 before releasing 2.98.0 (#8263)\n- Clarify Desktop startup safety and mask OAuth account labels (#8271)\n- Show app breakdowns and client chips (#8282)\n- Promote frozen tip de411020ed to main as 2.99.0 (#8322)\n\n## Changelog\n\nFull Changelog: https://github.com/lidge-jun/opencodex/compare/v2.98.0...v2.99.0\n\n- #8020 fix(anthropic): batch affinity writes and confirm operator resets @luvs01\n- #8053 feat(messaging): add opt-in stored Codex turn reply reads @HojooonKim\n- #8140 perf(kiro): count streamed tool argument bytes incrementally @0disoft\n- #8146 fix(responses): preserve mandatory tool choices through routing and recovery @luvs01\n- #8147 fix(ollama): bound tool-call validation and document request limits @luvs01\n- #8149 fix(workflows): enforce root send ceilings at physical admission @luvs01\n- #8176 test: stabilize Windows fixture setup and source checks @luvs01\n- #8229 test: bound Windows overflow slices and preserve child cleanup @lidge-jun\n- #8230 fix(responses): preserve late Devin signatures for DSH clients @salihozkara\n- #8235 fix(qoder): accept unambiguous selected tool aliases @juzijia\n- #8242 test(config): include uninstall refusal reason in regression output @luvs01\n- #8259 fix(mistral): ship per-model effort ladders and fold native Chat ultra @lidge-jun\n- #8261 fix(link): hedge leftover-pin refusal and count in-flight readiness reads @lidge-jun\n- #8263 chore(release): open dev at 2.99.0 before releasing 2.98.0 @github-actions[bot]\n- #8269 Fix dashboard switch and combo layout regressions @lidge-jun\n- #8271 Clarify Desktop startup safety and mask OAuth account labels @lidge-jun\n- #8272 Fix clipped Models rows and dashboard control layout @lidge-jun\n- #8277 perf(command-code): measure fragmented NDJSON incrementally @0disoft\n- #8278 fix(mistral): sanitize Chat fields and normalize native thinking content @lidge-jun\n- #8279 Fix omitted effort on dual-control Chat wires @lidge-jun\n- #8282 Show app breakdowns and client chips @lidge-jun\n- #8283 test: isolate Codex CLI update fixture process scans @lidge-jun\n- #8284 Honor max omission before native ultra clamping @lidge-jun\n- #8285 fix(desktop,gui): align macOS traffic lights on Sequoia and keep chips rounded in WKWebView @lidge-jun\n- #8289 Fix launcher signal race and chat-completions network flake @lidge-jun\n- #8316 fix(privacy): keep masked account label validation linear @lidge-jun\n- #8322 release: promote frozen tip de411020ed to main as 2.99.0 @lidge-jun\n\n## Code signing\n\nWindows binaries follow the [code signing policy](https://opencodex.me/reference/code-signing/).\nFree code signing provided by [SignPath.io](https://about.signpath.io/), certificate by [SignPath Foundation](https://signpath.org/).\n","mentions_count":6}